From 26e2691456cc7024eccbeb26cfbc8e534229a859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Komal Bajaj <komal.bajaj@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] FROMLIST: arm64: dts: qcom: shikra: Add EL2 overlay for
 remoteproc SMMU mappings

Shikra boards currently boot Linux under a hypervisor, where the remote
processor firmware IOMMU streams are managed by the hypervisor. When
booting Linux directly at EL2 without the hypervisor, the IOMMU is
instead managed by the consumer of this DeviceTree, so the firmware
streams for each remote processor need to be described explicitly.

Add an EL2-specific DT overlay and apply it to all Shikra EVK variants
to produce an -el2.dtb alongside the normal DTB. For the q6apm DAI,
replace the reserved-memory configuration with the apps SMMU stream
description used when Linux owns the SMMU at EL2.

Co-developed-by: Bibek Kumar Patro <bibek.patro@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Bibek Kumar Patro <bibek.patro@oss.qualcomm.com>
Co-developed-by: Mohit Sharma <mohit.sharma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Mohit Sharma <mohit.sharma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Co-developed-by: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261119-shikra-el2-v6-4-0e91a1467e79@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: Komal Bajaj <komal.bajaj@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso
index 8bbf099e9d5e3..d6fd98f23510f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso
@@ -33,3 +33,8 @@
 		iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x01a2 0x0001>;
 	};
 };
+
+&q6apmdai {
+	/delete-property/ memory-region;
+	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x01cc 0x3>;
+};
